    <bpmn:process id="W_W251" name="W251. Philippine Statutory Benefits &amp; Claims Administration (SSS, PhilHealth, Pag-IBIG)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Employee sickness event, maternity event, or application for SSS/Pag-IBIG statutory loan
Frequency: Continuous; daily processing of claims and semi-monthly reconciliation
Volume: 6,911 employee base; average ~120–180 sickness claims/month, ~40–60 maternity leaves/month, and ~250–350 loan applications/month
Owner: HR Benefits Specialist
Participants: Employee, HR Benefits Specialist, Payroll Specialist, Finance (Treasury)
Source: workflow W251 — Philippine Statutory Benefits &amp; Claims Administration (SSS, PhilHealth, Pag-IBIG)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W251_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W251_Lane1" name="Employee">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W251_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W251_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W251_Lane2" name="HR Benefits">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W251_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W251_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W251_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W251_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W251_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W251_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W251_Lane4" name="Payroll Spec">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W251_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W251_Lane5" name="Treasury">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W251_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W251_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W251_Start7" name="Employee sickness event, maternity event, or application for SSS/Pag-IBIG statutory loan">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W251_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W251_Task8" name="Claim Submission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Claim Submission: Employee uploads medical certificate, SSS Maternity Notification, or loan request documents to the HRIS/ERP system via Employee Self-Service (ESS) portal (W251.1)
Responsible (R): Employee
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W251_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W251_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W251_Task9" name="Eligibility Verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Eligibility Verification: HR Benefits Specialist reviews the uploaded documents; system auto-checks employee contribution history against SSS/PhilHealth criteria to verify eligibility (W251.2)
Responsible (R): HR Benefits
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W251_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W251_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W251_Task10" name="Agency Portal Certification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Agency Portal Certification: HR Benefits Specialist logs into the government agency&#x27;s online portal (SSS Sickness/Maternity portal, Pag-IBIG Virtual Employer portal) to certify the employee&#x27;s leave or confirm the employer endorsement for a salary/calamity loan (W251.3)
Responsible (R): HR Benefits
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W251_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W251_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W251_Task11" name="Benefit Advance Computation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Benefit Advance Computation: For SSS Sickness/Maternity, under Philippine law, the employer must advance the SSS benefit. System automatically computes the daily SSS benefit rate based on the employee&#x27;s average daily salary credit and schedules the advance payment (W251.4)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Payroll Mgr
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W251_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W251_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W251_Task12" name="Payroll Disbursal">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Payroll Disbursal: Payroll Specialist reviews the computed statutory advance and approves it for inclusion in the next semi-monthly payroll run (W10) (W251.5)
Responsible (R): Payroll Spec
Accountable (A): Payroll Mgr
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W251_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W251_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W251_Task13" name="Reimbursement Claim Submission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Reimbursement Claim Submission: After the employee returns or the leave completes, HR Benefits Specialist submits a digitized SSS Reimbursement Claim via the online portal to recover the advanced amount from the government (W251.6)
Responsible (R): HR Benefits
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W251_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W251_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W251_Task14" name="Reconciliation &amp; Settlement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Reconciliation &amp; Settlement: SSS releases the reimbursement via direct deposit to the company&#x27;s bank account. Finance reconciles the incoming bank settlement against the SSS Receivable ledger to close the transaction loop (W251.7)
Responsible (R): Treasury / Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W251_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W251_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W251_Task15" name="Loan Deduction Scheduling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Loan Deduction Scheduling: For SSS/Pag-IBIG loans, once approved, the system imports the monthly electronic billing files from SSS/Pag-IBIG, matches loan accounts with active employee profiles, and schedules the statutory semi-monthly deductions in the payroll system, ensuring compliance with minimum wage take-home pay rules (W251.8)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Payroll Mgr
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W251_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W251_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W251_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W251_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W251_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-296 (ensure controlled execution — Recruitment &amp; Onboarding (PA-19.1).) | - operational: updates
Owner: HR Benefits Specialist</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W251_Assoc18" sourceRef="W251_Annotation17" targetRef="W251_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W251_Flow19" sourceRef="W251_Start7" targetRef="W251_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W251_Flow20" sourceRef="W251_Task8" targetRef="W251_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W251_Flow21" sourceRef="W251_Task9" targetRef="W251_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W251_Flow22" sourceRef="W251_Task10" targetRef="W251_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W251_Flow23" sourceRef="W251_Task11" targetRef="W251_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W251_Flow24" sourceRef="W251_Task12" targetRef="W251_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W251_Flow25" sourceRef="W251_Task13" targetRef="W251_Task14" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W251_Flow26" sourceRef="W251_Task14" targetRef="W251_Task15" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W251_Flow27" sourceRef="W251_Task15" targetRef="W251_End16" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W251_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W251_plane" bpmnElement="W_W251">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W251_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W251_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="2000" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
