    <bpmn:process id="W_W777" name="W777. Employee Leave Balance Management &amp; Annual Leave Carry-Forward Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Semi-monthly payroll cycle; annual leave year-end processing
Frequency: Continuous (leave requests daily); monthly balance reconciliation; annual carry-forward (December)
Volume: 6,911 employees × ~4–6 leave requests/year = ~27,000–40,000 leave transactions/year
Owner: HR Business Partner
Participants: Employee, Direct Supervisor, HR Business Partner, Payroll Accountant
Source: workflow W777 — Employee Leave Balance Management &amp; Annual Leave Carry-Forward Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W777_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W777_Lane1" name="Employee">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W777_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W777_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W777_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W777_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W777_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W777_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W777_Lane3" name="Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W777_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W777_Lane4" name="HR BP">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W777_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W777_Lane5" name="Payroll Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W777_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W777_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W777_Start7" name="Semi-monthly payroll cycle; annual leave year-end processing">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W777_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W777_Task8" name="Leave request submission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Leave request submission: Employee submits leave request via self-service portal (HR-008) or mobile app: (a) leave type (VL, SL, SIL, maternity, paternity, solo parent, bereavement, others per HR-007), (b) start and end dates, (c) reason (confidential for SL), (d) contact during leave
Responsible (R): Employee
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W777_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W777_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W777_Task9" name="Balance and eligibility check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Balance and eligibility check: System validates: (a) leave type eligibility (SL requires medical certificate for &gt; 2 days per policy), (b) available balance, (c) probation period completed (VL not available during 6-month probation), (d) no conflicting approved leave for same dates, (e) department coverage verification (minimum staffing met per W34 scheduling)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Instant</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W777_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W777_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W777_Task10" name="Supervisor approval workflow">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Supervisor approval workflow: Direct Supervisor receives notification: (a) reviews request against department schedule per W34, (b) approves, modifies dates, or denies with reason, (c) for SL &gt; 3 days: requires supporting medical documentation upload, (d) system enforces approval SLA: 24 hours for standard, 4 hours for same-day emergency SL
Responsible (R): Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W777_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W777_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W777_Task11" name="Payroll integration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Payroll integration: Approved leave feeds to payroll per W10: (a) paid leave (VL, SL within balance): regular daily rate, (b) unpaid leave (beyond balance or LWOP): daily rate deduction per HR-010, (c) half-day SL: proportional deduction, (d) leave premium for regular holidays during VL period per HR-011
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Payroll Accountant
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W777_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W777_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W777_Task12" name="Monthly leave balance reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly leave balance reconciliation: HR Business Partner reviews: (a) leave accrual accuracy (1.25 days/month VL, 1.25 days/month SL), (b) negative leave balance flags (employee used more than accrued — requires recovery plan), (c) leave abuse patterns (&gt; 15 SL days/year, frequent Monday/Friday SL), (d) department leave utilization rates (target: 70-80% VL utilization for work-life balance)
Responsible (R): HR BP
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W777_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W777_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W777_Task13" name="Annual carry-forward processing (December)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Annual carry-forward processing (December): System performs year-end leave processing: (a) VL carry-forward: maximum 10 days (company policy — excess forfeited per policy communicated at hire), (b) SL carry-forward: up to 15 days (accumulates as emergency buffer), (c) SIL: statutory 5 days non-cumulative (use or convert to cash per DOLE rules), (d) generate employee leave balance statement for next year, (e) conversion of unused VL to cash for resigning/retiring employees per W643 final pay
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: Automated + 4 hours review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W777_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W777_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W777_Task14" name="Annual leave encashment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Annual leave encashment: For employees who qualify per policy: (a) excess VL beyond 10-day carry-forward converted to cash at daily rate, (b) SIL unused days converted to cash per Article 95 Labor Code, (c) encashment processed through December payroll per W10, (d) BIR withholding tax applied per TRAIN law graduated table
Responsible (R): Payroll Accountant
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: 2 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W777_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W777_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W777_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W777_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W777_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-296 (ensure controlled execution — Recruitment &amp; Onboarding (PA-19.1).) | - operational: must enforce entity-specific rules
Owner: HR Business Partner</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W777_Assoc17" sourceRef="W777_Annotation16" targetRef="W777_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W777_Flow18" sourceRef="W777_Start7" targetRef="W777_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W777_Flow19" sourceRef="W777_Task8" targetRef="W777_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W777_Flow20" sourceRef="W777_Task9" targetRef="W777_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W777_Flow21" sourceRef="W777_Task10" targetRef="W777_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W777_Flow22" sourceRef="W777_Task11" targetRef="W777_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W777_Flow23" sourceRef="W777_Task12" targetRef="W777_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W777_Flow24" sourceRef="W777_Task13" targetRef="W777_Task14" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W777_Flow25" sourceRef="W777_Task14" targetRef="W777_End15" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W777_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W777_plane" bpmnElement="W_W777">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W777_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W777_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1790" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
