    <bpmn:process id="W_W1526" name="W1526. Store-Level Seasonal &amp; Project-Based Temporary Staff Hiring, Contract Management &amp; Separation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: (a) Approving typhoon season (Jun–Nov) staffing surge, (b) holiday season (Ber months Sep–Dec) traffic increase, (c) new store grand opening temporary staffing, (d) special project (inventory count, store reset, warehouse overflow)
Frequency: Seasonal: 2 major cycles/year (typhoon + holiday); project-based: ad-hoc ~4–6 times/year per store
Volume: ~10–20 temporary staff per store per seasonal cycle × 200 stores = ~2,000–4,000 seasonal hires/year; ~1–3 project-based hires per event
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, HR Business Partner, local DOLE (Department of Labor and Employment), temporary staff
Source: workflow W1526 — Store-Level Seasonal &amp; Project-Based Temporary Staff Hiring, Contract Management &amp; Separation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1526_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1526_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1526_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1526_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1526_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1526_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1526_Lane2" name="HR Business Partner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1526_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1526_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1526_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1526_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1526_Start4" name="(a) Approving typhoon season (Jun–Nov) staffing surge, (b) holiday season (Ber months…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1526_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1526_Task5" name="Temporary staffing request">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Temporary staffing request: (a) Store Manager identifies need: (i) reason (seasonal surge, holiday traffic, project, new store opening), (ii) number of temps needed, (iii) duration (start/end date), (iv) roles (stock associate, cashier helper, customer assistant, warehouse helper), (v) budget impact; (b) submits request to HR Business Partner for approval
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): HR Business Partner
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1526_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1526_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1526_Task6" name="Recruitment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Recruitment: (a) HR Business Partner recruits locally (within store&#x27;s community): (i) post at store entrance and barangay bulletin board, (ii) coordinate with local barangay employment desk (Philippine LGUs maintain local employment registries), (iii) tap walk-in applicants; (b) minimum qualifications: (i) 18 years old (DOLE minimum for non-hazardous work), (ii) physically fit (stock associate requires heavy lifting), (iii) no criminal record; (c) interview and selection by Store Manager
Responsible (R): HR Business Partner / Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1526_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1526_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1526_Task7" name="Contract execution and DOLE compliance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Contract execution and DOLE compliance: (a) HR Business Partner prepares employment contract: (i) contract type: &quot;Project Employment Contract&quot; or &quot;Seasonal Employment Contract&quot; per Labor Code provisions, (ii) specific project/season description, (iii) definite start and end date, (iv) daily wage rate (must meet regional minimum wage per RTWPB — Regional Tripartite Wages and Productivity Board rates vary by region), (v) no probationary period (temporary workers are not probationary employees), (vi) clear statement that employment ends on specified date or project completion; (b) employee signs contract; (c) HR Business Partner files: (i) DOLE-required employment report (RKS Form 5 — Report on Employment to DOLE Regional Office), (ii) employee master record created in payroll system with &quot;Project/Seasonal&quot; status
Responsible (R): HR Business Partner
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours per hire</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1526_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1526_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1526_Task8" name="Onboarding">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Onboarding (abbreviated vs. regular employee): (a) Store Manager conducts abbreviated orientation: (i) store layout and safety rules (1 hour), (ii) specific role training (cashier assist, stock handling, customer greeting — 2–4 hours), (iii) time clock/biometric registration, (iv) uniform/PPE issuance per W780; (b) no extensive onboarding program (vs. regular employees who receive full W37 onboarding); (c) temporary staff assigned a &quot;buddy&quot; from regular staff for first 3 days
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 3–5 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1526_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1526_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1526_Task9" name="Daily time and attendance management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Daily time and attendance management: (a) temporary staff clocks in/out via biometric (same as regular employees); (b) system tracks hours by project/seasonal code for proper cost allocation; (c) Store Manager approves daily timesheets; (d) overtime strictly managed: DOLE requires overtime pay (125% of hourly rate) for work beyond 8 hours/day — temporary workers must not exceed regular overtime limits
Responsible (R): Store Manager / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Daily</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1526_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1526_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1526_Task10" name="End-of-contract separation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: End-of-contract separation: (a) on contract end date: (i) Store Manager conducts brief exit meeting: confirm project/season completed, collect uniform/PPE, sign clearance form; (ii) HR Business Partner processes final pay: (a) last salary, (b) proportionate 13th month pay (per PD 851: all employees including seasonal receive 13th month pay proportionate to months worked), (c) SIL (Service Incentive Leave) conversion if applicable (after 12 months of service — seasonal workers rarely qualify); (iii) system updates employee status to &quot;Separated — End of Contract&quot;; (b) DOLE notice: HR Business Partner files termination report with DOLE Regional Office within 30 days of separation; (c) important: no re-hire of same seasonal worker within 6 months without converting to regular status (DOLE constructive regularization doctrine)
Responsible (R): HR Business Partner / Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1–2 hours per separation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1526_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1526_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1526_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1526_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1526_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-296 (ensure controlled execution — Recruitment &amp; Onboarding (PA-19.1).) | - operational: Store Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1526_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1526_Annotation12" targetRef="W1526_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1526_Flow14" sourceRef="W1526_Start4" targetRef="W1526_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1526_Flow15" sourceRef="W1526_Task5" targetRef="W1526_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1526_Flow16" sourceRef="W1526_Task6" targetRef="W1526_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1526_Flow17" sourceRef="W1526_Task7" targetRef="W1526_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1526_Flow18" sourceRef="W1526_Task8" targetRef="W1526_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1526_Flow19" sourceRef="W1526_Task9" targetRef="W1526_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1526_Flow20" sourceRef="W1526_Task10" targetRef="W1526_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1526_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1526_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1526">
