    <bpmn:process id="W_W5551" name="W5551. Employee Arrest, Detention &amp; Criminal-Case Employment-Status Response Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: An employee is arrested, detained, or formally charged with a crime — whether arising from work (a fleet accident per W653, a loss-prevention case per W839, an on-duty incident per W717/W471) or from private life — so the employment-status, legal-support, payroll-continuity and family-liaison response must run before any court outcome
Frequency: Occasional-to-rare; ~6–10 events/year chain-wide across ~6,911 employees (driver reckless-imprudence cases dominating, plus LP-referred arrests and off-duty detentions)
Volume: 1 event × the affected employee × a decision surface spanning payroll continuity, statutory benefits (W251), the employee&#x27;s family, the sponsoring manager, and the work-relatedness determination that fixes who pays for counsel
Owner: HR Manager (case mechanic); VP Legal &amp; Compliance (work-related legal posture)
Participants: HR Business Partner, VP Legal, Outside Counsel, Fleet Safety Officer (driver cases per W653), LP Director (LP-origin cases per W839/W471), Payroll Manager (W10/W641), HR Benefits, Store/DC Manager, CHRO, Labor Relations Director where the employee is union-covered (VS-84)
Source: workflow W5551 — Employee Arrest, Detention &amp; Criminal-Case Employment-Status Response Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5551_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5551_Lane1" name="HR Business Partner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5551_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5551_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5551_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5551_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5551_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5551_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5551_Lane2" name="HR Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5551_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5551_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5551_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5551_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5551_Start4" name="An employee is arrested, detained, or formally charged with a crime — whether arising…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5551_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5551_Task5" name="Intake &amp; verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Intake &amp; verification: confirm the detention through counsel or the family — never through rumor or social media; identify the charging offense, arresting unit, detention facility, bail status, and next hearing; open a restricted-access case file (criminal-case information is sensitive personal information under the W647/VS-91 privacy canon)
Responsible (R): HR Business Partner / VP Legal
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: &lt; 24 h</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5551_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5551_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5551_Task6" name="Work-relatedness classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Work-relatedness classification: (a) work-connected (on-duty conduct, company vehicle, company premises, LP-referred case): company counsel engaged, the W653/W839/W471 chains linked, and the employer-liability assessment opened (Arts. 2176/2180 exposure; vehicle recovery; insurance notification); (b) private-life case: employment handled on its own footing, company legal support decided case-by-case
Responsible (R): HR Business Partner / VP Legal
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 1–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5551_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5551_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5551_Task7" name="Employment-status placement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Employment-status placement: place the employee on leave of absence for the detention period — no automatic termination, no abandonment finding while detained (the absence is involuntary); preventive suspension only where the charge is work-connected and continued presence is a risk (W2883 rules, 30-day cap); status letter served to the last-known address with family acknowledgment
Responsible (R): HR Business Partner
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: 2–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5551_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5551_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5551_Task8" name="Payroll, benefits &amp; family liaison">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Payroll, benefits &amp; family liaison: payroll stopped per leave rules with a written computation handed to the family; SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG continuity elections per W251; one named HR family liaison; emergency-assistance evaluation per the W994 no-interest-loan class and W2865 counseling access for the family
Responsible (R): HR Business Partner / Payroll Manager / HR Benefits
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5551_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5551_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5551_Task9" name="Case-milestone cadence">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Case-milestone cadence: bail, arraignment and hearings tracked through counsel; 30/60/90-day status reviews of the placement — prolonged detention is a status-review trigger, not a termination trigger; union/LMC notification where the employee is covered (W2880)
Responsible (R): HR Business Partner / Outside Counsel
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5551_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5551_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5551_Task10" name="Resolution — favorable outcome">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Resolution — favorable outcome: acquittal or case dismissal → reinstate to the same or a substantially equivalent position where one exists; re-onboarding rides W15; no trace of the charge in the promotability or succession record
Responsible (R): HR Manager / HR Business Partner
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5551_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5551_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5551_Task11" name="Resolution — conviction or just-cause finding">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Resolution — conviction or just-cause finding: run the W2883/W2884 two-notice machinery on the verified facts — the conviction or the conduct it proves is the cause, never the arrest; clearance, final pay and COE wording per the separation chains; NLRC exposure managed per W2885/W2886/W2887
Responsible (R): HR Manager / VP Legal
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5551_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5551_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5551_Task12" name="Records, privacy &amp; register">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Records, privacy &amp; register: close the restricted case file on the records-retention schedule; anonymized entry in the labor-relations risk register (W2895); lessons-learned only where a company control failed (e.g., the W653 driver-training chain feeding a fleet fix)
Responsible (R): HR Manager / VP Legal
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5551_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5551_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5551_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5551_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5551_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-296 (ensure controlled execution — Recruitment &amp; Onboarding (PA-19.1).) | - CTL-217 (ensure labor-relations statutory compliance.) | - operational: no separation letter issues on the fact of arrest alone — every termination decision routes W2883/W2884 with counsel sign-off; reinstatement after acquittal is offered in writing
Owner: HR Manager (case mechanic); VP Legal &amp; Compliance (work-related legal posture)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5551_Assoc15" sourceRef="W5551_Annotation14" targetRef="W5551_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5551_Flow16" sourceRef="W5551_Start4" targetRef="W5551_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5551_Flow17" sourceRef="W5551_Task5" targetRef="W5551_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5551_Flow18" sourceRef="W5551_Task6" targetRef="W5551_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5551_Flow19" sourceRef="W5551_Task7" targetRef="W5551_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5551_Flow20" sourceRef="W5551_Task8" targetRef="W5551_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5551_Flow21" sourceRef="W5551_Task9" targetRef="W5551_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5551_Flow22" sourceRef="W5551_Task10" targetRef="W5551_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5551_Flow23" sourceRef="W5551_Task11" targetRef="W5551_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5551_Flow24" sourceRef="W5551_Task12" targetRef="W5551_End13" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W5551_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W5551_plane" bpmnElement="W_W5551">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W5551_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W5551_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="2000" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W5551_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W5551_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="2000" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W5551_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W5551_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W5551_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W5551_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W5551_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W5551_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W5551_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W5551_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W5551_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W5551_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
